\@writefile{lof}{\defcounter {refsection}{0}\relax }\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Illustrative comparison of uncertainty estimation on 1D regression data with outliers. Row 1 shows data with no outliers while row 2 data contains 10\% outliers. The blue dots are clean data while red dots are outlier. The shaded blue region is the estimated uncertainty. Both Gaussian and Ensemble methods are more sensitive to outliers, the blue region are more distorted by the outlier data points, while for our generalized approach the blue region has distorted less indicating less impact of outliers.\relax }}{1}\protected@file@percent }
